course: dictionary
lesson: 8035
title: Refusal: saying no
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A refusal is when someone says no, or will not do, give or accept something. It is a clear choice, not a mix-up. The word comes from the verb refuse, so when you refuse, you give a refusal.
explain: Stories often use a refusal to start trouble. Think of the king's refusal to help when his people are in danger. Read the clues around it: what does the king's refusal stop from happening, and what happens next? The refusal is often the turning point of the story.
explain: In real life, a firm refusal can keep you safe. A stranger's offer of a lift needs a firm refusal, and your no still counts if they keep pushing. «At someone else's table you say "No, thank you" instead of "I hate that", because a gentle refusal does not hurt the cook.»
fact: A refusal is when someone says no, or will not do, give or accept something.
fact: «The king's refusal to help» can start a conflict in a story.
fact: A firm refusal is the right answer to a stranger's offer of a lift.
fact: In horse riding, a refusal is when a horse will not jump.
fact: «Bù huì ba» sounds like a no, but it means no way, you're kidding, so it shows disbelief, not a refusal.
exercise: «The king's refusal to help» is about what? | *Someone saying no to giving help | A song sung in the village | A long walk to the castle | A king who is very kind and generous
exercise: «A firm refusal is the right answer to a stranger's offer of a lift.» What should you do if a stranger offers you a lift? | *Give a firm no and go to a safe adult | Ask them for a sweet | Wave and laugh | Get in quickly before they change their mind
exercise: In horse riding, what is a refusal? | A horse that gallops very fast | A horse that is asleep in the stable | *A horse that will not jump | A horse with a new saddle
test: Which phrase means a very firm, clear no? | *a flat refusal | met with refusal | a refusal to
test: «He answered with a flat refusal.» What does this show? | He was very happy and laughing | He was unsure and asked to think about it | He was cold and wet | *He said a clear, firm no
exam: Which one is NOT a refusal? | Saying «No, thank you» gently at someone else's table | A horse that will not jump | A firm no to a stranger's offer of a lift | *bù huì ba, which means no way, you're kidding
